    {
      "id": "chem24-exothermic-endothermic",
      "title": "Exothermic and endothermic changes",
      "summary": "Follow the temperature of four changes in a polystyrene cup (neutralisation, ammonium nitrate dissolving, citric acid with sodium hydrogencarbonate, magnesium in acid) and decide which give out heat and which take it in.",
      "briefing": "An exothermic change gives out heat to its surroundings, so the solution warms; an endothermic one takes heat in, so it cools. Read the temperature before and after each change.",
